  "body": "Large updates to DOM can be causes of jank that are unavoidable from the developer's point of view, because DOM is synchronous and atomic. We would like to provide the developer with an API that allows them to lock an element's subtree for display, allowing the possibility for script and the user-agent to co-operatively process DOM updates, style, layout and paint, with a promise callback informing the developer when the work is done. \r\n \r\nWe're calling this display locking, and we have a WICG thread going into far more detail here:\r\nhttps://discourse.wicg.io/t/proposal-display-locking/2905\r\n\r\nShould this feature go forward, it will likely be added to the HTML spec. We'd like to gather feedback early on from both developers and user-agents about viability and desirability of this feature.\r\n\r\n/cc @chrishtr\r\n",
